1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:17,599
Victor Voltage called while I was in the bath. I answered because some
niggas only call from the sky when the sky is about to become a
problem. "Aiden," he said, "how attached are you to that hotel roof?"
I sat up. Shawna looked over from the mirror.

2
00:00:17,849 --> 00:00:40,770
She had one earring in and the expression of a woman whose husband had
just heard the opening sentence of another emergency. "What happened?"
I asked. "Minor difficulty with the aircraft." Behind him, somebody
shouted, "WE HAVE LOST THE OTHER ENGINE!" Victor covered the phone
badly. "I am talking to Aiden!" I stood, water running off me.

3
00:00:41,020 --> 00:01:02,951
"Nigga, what other engine?" "The second one." "How many did you start
with?" "Two." Shawna threw me a towel. "Tell him breakfast is getting
cold." I heard Seraphine Storm's voice over the phone, calm enough to
make the shouting around her sound rude. "Captain, we are over the
western quarter. The emperor's men have fired upon our transport.

4
00:01:03,201 --> 00:01:25,489
Victor has kept us aloft longer than the pilot believed possible. He
has approximately three minutes of strength left." "What you flying?"
"A university transport." "How big?" "We brought gifts." Nigga, I knew
then it was a big fucking plane. I dressed in pieces while running.
Shawna buttoned my shirt in the elevator.

5
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:45,912
Tank met us in the lobby carrying two coffees and a gun bag. He looked
at my wet hair. "You shower during that phone call?" "Other way
around." June was already outside, staring west. A white aircraft hung
above the city with one wing trailing smoke. Lightning flashed around
its nose.

6
00:01:46,162 --> 00:02:09,055
Victor was somewhere up there putting his whole body between a school
full of presents and the ground. Seraphine came back on the phone.
"There is an unfinished exhibition hall south of your hotel. Its roof
is broad enough for an emergency landing, but there are cranes in the
approach." I looked at June. She pointed before I asked. "Glass
building.

7
00:02:09,304 --> 00:02:28,596
Half mile." "Get everybody out of its way." "Everybody?" "Nigga, the
plane got gifts." We took the silver Chrome Special because it was
closest and because a nigga should occasionally thank a friend by
putting his gift through terrible stress. Shawna came with me. Tank
and June followed.

8
00:02:28,846 --> 00:02:48,324
The morning traffic scattered around our lights, drivers leaning out
to cheer until they looked up and remembered the sky could fall. The
exhibition hall stood beside a dry canal. Its enormous roof shone
beneath three construction cranes. Workers ran across the forecourt,
pointing at the plane.

9
00:02:48,574 --> 00:03:09,113
A security guard tried to stop me at the entrance, saw the aircraft,
and decided his barrier did not pay enough. I drove straight into the
hall. The place was empty except for scaffolding, marble crates, and a
ridiculous gold model of Zero's palace. My tires squealed across
polished stone.

10
00:03:09,363 --> 00:03:33,243
We went through a set of unfinished doors and onto a sloping service
ramp that climbed toward the roof. Shawna held the dashboard. "Does
this go all the way?" "About to." "Aiden." "Baby, I got confidence."
"I would love some information to go with it." The ramp ended on an
open terrace one floor below the roof. For a second, I had too much
information.

11
00:03:33,493 --> 00:03:54,023
Then I saw the scaffolding bridge connecting the terrace to the crane
platform. "There." "That isn't a road." "Nigga, it is today." We hit
the narrow bridge. Metal shuddered beneath the tires. A board snapped
behind us. I kept the car straight while Shawna watched the far end
with her jaw set.

12
00:03:54,273 --> 00:04:17,846
We climbed onto the crane platform just as the plane dropped low
enough to blot out the sun. Victor hung beneath its nose, bright with
electricity, one hand braced against the fuselage. His whole body
shook. I could see him now. The nigga looked like a man trying to
bench-press a terrible decision made by an airline. "Victor!" He
turned his head.

13
00:04:18,096 --> 00:04:39,103
Even from up there, I saw him grin. "You brought the new car!"
"Cassius gonna be pissed if you land on it!" The plane lurched.
Victor's grin vanished. I could not hold a plane. Blue Thunder did not
make me a god. It gave me a few fierce moments when my body could
conduct something stronger than it ought to survive.

14
00:04:39,353 --> 00:04:57,900
I had learned the price at Sky High. Every time I spent it, my hands
shook afterward like the strength had taken the bones with it. But I
could give my friend a moment. I looked at Shawna. She already knew.
"Enough to help him," she said. "Then you let go." I kissed her once.

15
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:19,302
"Get down behind the wall." She got out, took the emergency flare from
the car, and ran toward the roof's far edge to guide the pilot. I
stepped onto the hood. Blue light crawled between my fingers. Nigga,
it hurt before it became beautiful. The old scar in my side tightened.
My teeth pressed together.

16
00:05:19,552 --> 00:05:38,850
I reached up as Victor brought the plane over the crane platform, low
enough that its belly filled my world. For one breath our hands met.
His lightning met mine. The air cracked blue. The plane lifted just
enough to clear the first crane. Victor shouted. I shouted back.

17
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:59,317
There was no clever shit in it, no king speech, just two niggas
refusing to let go of their people at the same time. Then I pushed the
last of my charge through him and dropped to one knee on the hood.
"Go!" Victor moved with the aircraft. Its wheels struck the broad roof
hard enough to throw dust from the seams.

18
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:19,998
Shawna stood at the far end waving the flare. The pilot turned toward
her light. One wing clipped a hanging sheet of construction fabric.
The fabric wrapped around it like a bride's veil on the ugliest
wedding of all time. The plane slid. A crane cable snapped. I heard
Tank yelling below.

19
00:06:20,248 --> 00:06:44,022
The aircraft stopped with its nose hanging over the far edge of the
roof. For a second, nothing moved. Then its door opened. Dean
Seraphine Storm stepped out wearing a white traveling suit and
carrying a bouquet. She looked across the roof at me kneeling on a
silver car. "Captain," she called, "your practical work remains
exceptional." I tried to answer.

20
00:06:44,272 --> 00:07:06,274
What came out was mostly breathing. Shawna ran back to me. She caught
my elbow before I could pretend I did not need help. "Sit." "I am
sitting." "On the ground. You keep choosing expensive things to
collapse on." She got me off the hood and into the passenger seat. My
hands trembled so badly she had to open the water bottle for me.

21
00:07:06,524 --> 00:07:25,219
I hated that. I loved that she did it without turning it into a
speech. Victor stumbled across the roof toward us. His uniform was
scorched. His hair stood up in seven directions, six of which appeared
physically impossible. He bent and hugged me through the open door.

22
00:07:25,469 --> 00:07:44,270
"My nigga." "You heavy as shit." "That is gratitude you feel." "Feels
like a grown man in my lap." Shawna laughed, and Victor laughed, and
for a moment the fact that we were all alive was loud enough to drown
out the broken plane. Then bullets struck the roof wall. Of course.

23
00:07:44,520 --> 00:08:07,890
Zero's niggas could not allow a reunion to have decent lighting
without firing at it. Black Mantle guards were climbing the service
stairs on the far side of the building. More vehicles stopped in the
forecourt below. They had watched the plane come down and come to
collect whatever survived. Seraphine set the bouquet carefully inside
the plane's doorway.

24
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:32,104
"Victor," she said, "rest." "Dean, I can—" "That was not a question."
She raised one hand. The air above the roof tightened. Loose cloth
lifted. Dust spun into a pale circle around her shoes. The first guard
reached the stair top and found the wind had opinions about his
arrival. He flew backward into the men behind him. Their guns
clattered down the steps.

25
00:08:32,354 --> 00:08:56,210
Tank appeared at the other staircase with Rosa and June behind him.
"Aiden! How many fucking floors you need?" "Ask the architect!" He ran
to the plane. Rosa followed with a medical bag she had taken from Vega
downstairs. I had not even seen the doctor arrive; apparently she had
been summoned by the universal signal of me doing something stupid at
altitude.

26
00:08:56,460 --> 00:09:23,035
Passengers began coming out of the transport. All grown, all rattled.
A Sky High music instructor carried two instrument cases. A faculty
cook held a covered tray against his chest. An enormous instructor in
a purple coat emerged with a wedding cake box so large it needed
handles. "That better not be our cake," Rosa said. "A sample," the
cook replied, offended.

27
00:09:23,285 --> 00:09:45,571
"The final cake would never travel in these conditions." Tank stared
at the box. "Nigga, that's a sample?" I laughed, then regretted
laughing because every muscle in my chest had joined a union against
me. The guards fired again from a neighboring rooftop. Seraphine
turned, keeping the wind between the passengers and the shots.

28
00:09:45,821 --> 00:10:08,138
She could protect the roof or help unload the plane, but not both
forever. Victor tried to stand. Shawna pushed him back beside me. "You
two saved it once. Let somebody else have a fucking turn." Then she
took my gun bag and went to Tank. My wife and my brother moved to the
far wall together. Tank covered the neighboring roof.

29
00:10:08,388 --> 00:10:30,168
Shawna fired at the light above its doorway, bursting the glass and
forcing the guards back into the dark stairwell behind it. June found
a construction cart and began loading cases onto it. Rosa got the
shaken passengers moving toward our stairs, speaking to them like they
were late for rehearsal and she would not accept excuses.

30
00:10:30,418 --> 00:10:54,385
I watched the people I loved handle the world while my hands shook in
my lap. Victor sat beside me on the pavement, leaning against the
tire. "It is difficult," he said. "What?" "Being temporarily less
impressive." "Speak for yourself. I'm still handsome." "Yes. It is
extremely irritating." I held out the water. He drank, wiped his
mouth, and passed it back.

31
00:10:54,635 --> 00:11:10,435
"You knew I'd come?" he asked. "To the desert?" "To the end." I looked
at him. Under the scorched uniform and ridiculous hair was the same
proud nigga who had once wanted to beat me so badly he could barely
stand beside me.

32
00:11:10,685 --> 00:11:31,073
Now he had crossed an ocean in a plane full of wedding presents
because he knew I was walking into the last fight. "Yeah," I said. "I
knew." He nodded once. Then the nigga pointed at my wet hair. "You
were bathing when I called." "Yeah." "My nigga got out of a bath to
save me." "Nigga, there was an entire plane.

33
00:11:31,323 --> 00:11:51,987
Don't make this sound like you needed help reaching a towel." "And you
weren't even dry." "Victor." "The academy must know." "The academy can
know you started with two engines and arrived borrowing mine." He
laughed, then grabbed his ribs. I passed him the water. His hands
still trembled, just less than before.

34
00:11:52,237 --> 00:12:16,530
The nigga had earned every stupid sentence he could get out between
breaths. "They'll have to alter the painting," he said. I looked at
him. "What painting?" "Dean Storm commissioned your portrait. Captain
Aiden above the clouds." "Nigga, what am I wearing?" "Your uniform."
"Good. You keep telling bath stories, some nigga gonna hang my ass
beside the attendance office." Victor tried to stop laughing.

35
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:43,939
Failed. Waved the bottle at me like that would make it my
responsibility. "They argued over the inscription." "How long?" "Forty
minutes." "Nigga, I almost died in less. What won?" "A Man Above Us
All." I nodded. "Accurate faculty." "One professor suggested
Outstanding Attendance." "That nigga understands the material." "Then
they argued over how much larger than life to make you." "Start with
actual size.

36
00:12:44,189 --> 00:13:08,537
Tell those niggas to bring a longer wall." Victor leaned against the
tire, smiling with his eyes shut. I let him rest. Behind us the ruined
plane ticked and settled; somewhere a crate scraped over concrete,
somebody helping somebody else lift it. Our friends still had work to
do while we sat here being grateful badly. He passed the water back.
"Thank you," he said.

37
00:13:08,787 --> 00:13:32,701
No painting in it now. Just him. "My nigga." I drank. My hands were
steadier too. Two exhausted niggas under a plane, spending the
strength we had left on making each other laugh. I would've come out
of a thousand baths for that. Down below, an armored truck crashed
through the exhibition hall's front doors. The floor shook. June
looked over the edge and swore.

38
00:13:32,951 --> 00:13:57,769
"They're inside." The stairs were our way out. The guards were coming
up them. Seraphine's wind lashed the roof, but she could not reach
inside the building without letting the shooters across the street
have us. I flexed my fingers. Nothing. No blue light. Only pain and a
weak twitch. Shawna saw. "Don't." "I wasn't." "I know your face."
"Nigga, everybody knows my face.

39
00:13:58,019 --> 00:14:22,422
It's famous." She ignored that and pointed at the silver car. "Can you
drive?" I looked from the car to the scaffolding bridge. "With you
yelling directions?" "Always." We loaded the most shaken passengers
into the faculty transport carts that had come out of the cargo hold.
Of course Sky High had brought little electric cars inside its big
electric emergency.

40
00:14:22,672 --> 00:14:47,327
Seraphine covered their crossing as June drove the first one onto the
scaffolding bridge. Tank carried the cake sample himself, because some
priorities survive war. Shawna got behind the wheel of my silver car.
"Move over." I obeyed. Nigga, loving a woman gives her certain
privileges over your most expensive possessions and all your least
sensible ideas.

41
00:14:47,577 --> 00:15:10,606
She drove us across the swaying bridge while bullets chipped the
concrete behind us. Victor lay across the back seats muttering that he
would never complain about legroom again. At the terrace, Shawna
turned sharply down the ramp. Below, the armored truck blocked the
exhibition hall. Its driver saw us coming and swung toward the ramp.
Shawna did not slow.

42
00:15:10,856 --> 00:15:34,828
"Baby." "I see him." "Baby." "I married you. I know a bad approach
when I see one." She drove up the sloping side of a marble crate. The
silver car tilted onto two wheels. For one impossible second we
balanced against the crate while the armored truck passed beneath our
raised side. I could see the driver's astonished face through his
windshield.

43
00:15:35,078 --> 00:15:54,013
He looked at my wife like he had just discovered a second Aiden and
did not have enough bullets for the information. Then we landed on all
four tires and tore through the hall's broken doors. Victor sat up
just enough to shout. "Mrs. Aiden!" "Seat belt!" she shouted back.

44
00:15:54,263 --> 00:16:16,514
We reached the hotel with our people, the gifts, the cake sample, and
a piece of the plane's fabric still caught in Tank's collar. The
courtyard filled with cheers. Cassius ran toward the silver car, saw
the new scratches, and put a hand over his heart. "My gift." "Your
gift saved a plane," I told him. He looked at Shawna. She raised an
eyebrow.

45
00:16:16,764 --> 00:16:36,883
"And I drove it home." Cassius bowed so deeply Inez slapped the back
of his head. Vega made me sit in a quiet room with Victor for an hour.
She examined my hands, checked my pulse, and told me that if I tried
to summon more lightning before I could hold a glass steadily, she
would have Tank sit on me.

46
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:57,375
"That medically necessary?" I asked. "For my peace of mind." Seraphine
came in carrying the bouquet from the plane. Somehow it had survived
with only three petals missing. She placed it in Shawna's hands. "For
your wedding renewal. I wished to bring them personally." Shawna
looked down at the flowers.

47
00:16:57,625 --> 00:17:19,996
"You could have mailed them." "My dear, your husband would have found
that insufficiently dramatic." I lifted a finger. "She's right." The
dean turned to me. Her expression softened. "You have assembled a
remarkable family, Captain." Through the open door, I could hear Tank
arguing that a sample cake should be sampled by somebody. Rosa was
defending it.

48
00:17:20,246 --> 00:17:44,669
Mercedes was asking the music instructor if he knew anything filthy.
Porsche was telling the hotel owner that a rooftop piano would improve
the mood. June and Adrian were describing Shawna's two-wheel stunt to
Inez, who kept looking into the room at my wife with growing
professional respect. "Yeah," I said. "I know." Seraphine took a
sealed envelope from her coat.

49
00:17:44,919 --> 00:18:07,516
"The academy sent something else." I opened it. A photograph slid out:
Sky High floating above the clouds, our whole class on the steps, me
in the center wearing the captain's badge like the school had been
built around it. On the back, every instructor had signed a message.
At the bottom, Victor had written one line larger than the rest.

50
00:18:07,766 --> 00:18:31,652
IF HE GETS HIMSELF KILLED, I AM GOING TO BE VERY ANGRY. I looked at
him across the room. The nigga shrugged. "Motivation." I folded the
photograph carefully and put it inside my jacket, beside the cross. A
siren sounded in the courtyard. Not the emperor's siren. Mine had a
different kind of arrogance. I went to the window with Shawna's hand
on my elbow.

51
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:53,832
Six dark-blue vehicles rolled through the hotel gates, their lights
spinning over the palms. The lead car stopped beside my Lamborghini.
Chief Gloria Knox stepped out wearing a white uniform, a gold badge,
and sunglasses that reflected an entire hotel full of her favorite
mistakes. She looked up at the window.

52
00:18:54,082 --> 00:19:19,546
"Captain!" "Chief!" "Why is there an airplane on a shopping center?"
"Exhibition hall!" "That clears it right up!" She came upstairs with
two officers carrying suitcases. One case held clothes. The other held
a ceremonial sword that Las Vegas apparently believed I needed because
regular weapons had failed to express its affection. Knox embraced
Shawna first.

53
00:19:19,796 --> 00:19:33,406
Then she took my face between both hands and examined me like a mother
who had raised a department instead of a child. "You look tired."
"Saved a plane." "I saw. Somebody filmed you from a crane.

54
00:19:33,656 --> 00:19:54,180
The city council watched it six times." "They should've been helping."
"They voted to name a road after you." "I already got one." "They
voted for a better road." Victor laughed from the couch. Knox looked
at him. "And you're the young man who held it up." He sat straighter.
"Victor Voltage." "Excellent work.

55
00:19:54,430 --> 00:20:11,892
We are considering a roundabout." "I would accept a tasteful one." She
nodded seriously, then turned back to me. "I brought twelve
volunteers. All grown, all armed, all aware you attract trouble like a
free bar attracts off-duty police.

56
00:20:12,142 --> 00:20:34,591
They are downstairs helping your people secure the hotel." "Zero let
you through?" "He tried to charge an arrival tax." "You pay it?" She
stared at me over her sunglasses. Nigga, I had forgotten who I was
talking to. "The border captain now owes me money," she said. Shawna
laughed and hugged her again. Knox set the sword on the table.

57
00:20:34,841 --> 00:20:57,298
Its scabbard was blue velvet. The hilt had my initials worked into
gold. I lifted it halfway, saw my reflection in the polished blade,
and understood why old kings had difficulty being reasonable. "The
city wanted you to have something dignified," she said. "Nigga, this
is a sword with my name on it." "I argued for two.

58
00:20:57,548 --> 00:21:18,867
Budget hearing was difficult." She waited until the others began
discussing where to put the sword before lowering her voice. "I didn't
come for a photograph, Aiden." I looked at her. "I know." "You made my
department the most famous in the world. Half the applicants want to
be you. The other half want to arrest you and get promoted.

59
00:21:19,117 --> 00:21:36,074
I would prefer to keep the original alive." "Working on it." She
touched the badge on my chest. "Work harder. Your wife has plans."
Across the room, Shawna was showing Seraphine a photograph of the
dress she wanted for Vegas. Rosa had joined them.

60
00:21:36,324 --> 00:22:00,748
Three women leaned over a phone while a whole criminal empire waited
outside, and none of them looked remotely willing to postpone their
celebration. I looked back at Knox. "Yes, ma'am." She smiled. "There.
Best officer I ever hired. Follows instructions when properly
threatened." Outside, the sky was empty again. Our people had all come
down safely.
